        "n0023"
      ],
      "range": [
        "spya-hg7u0a",
        "spya-xk7vyy"
      ],
      "title": "Writes and write-nots",
      "gist": "As AI erases the middle ground, society will split into good writers and people who can't write at all, and since writing is thinking, this divide is really one of thinks and think-nots."
    },
    "n0020": {
      "id": "n0020",
      "depth": 2,
      "parent": "n0019",
      "children": [
        "n0021",
        "n0022"
      ],
      "range": [
        "spya-hg7u0a",
        "spya-z79mew"
      ],
      "title": "A vanishing middle ground",
      "gist": "Unlike the disappearance of obsolete skills like blacksmithing, the loss of ordinary writing ability matters because it removes a whole tier of competence."
    },
    "n0021": {
      "id": "n0021",
      "depth": 3,
